        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Grand Forks, Grand Forks County, North Dakota, El Paso, El Paso County, Texas, United States, Central El Paso, Downtown El Paso, Fort Bliss\n- Airports: Grand Forks International Airport, El Paso International Airport\n- Codes: IATA GFK, ICAO KGFK, FAA LID GFK, IATA ELP, ICAO KELP, FAA LID ELP\n\nFacts:\n- Grand Forks International Airport is a public airport located five miles northwest of Grand Forks in Grand Forks County, North Dakota.\n- Grand Forks International Airport uses IATA code GFK, ICAO code KGFK, and FAA LID GFK.\n- El Paso International Airport is a public airport located four miles northeast of downtown El Paso in El Paso County, Texas, United States.\n- El Paso International Airport uses IATA code ELP, ICAO code KELP, and FAA LID ELP.\n- Central El Paso is close to El Paso International Airport, Downtown El Paso, the international border, and Fort Bliss.",
